<section>
  <div class="content">
    <p>
      A pendulum wave is a device that demonstrates the relationship between period and length in simple pendulums. Each pendulum has a slightly different length, causing them to oscillate at slightly different frequencies. Over time, the pendulums cycle through synchronized motion, traveling wave patterns, apparent chaos, and back to synchronization.
    </p>

    <form>
      <label for="pendulum-count">
        Pendulums: <output id="pendulum-count-value">15</output>
        <input id="pendulum-count" type="range" min="5" max="30" value="15" step="1" aria-label="Number of pendulums">
      </label>
      <label for="speed">
        Speed: <output id="speed-value">0.2x</output>
        <input id="speed" type="range" min="0.05" max="1" value="0.2" step="0.05" aria-label="Simulation speed">
      </label>
      <label for="trails">
        <input id="trails" type="checkbox"> Trails
      </label>
      <span>
        <button id="pause-button" type="button">Pause</button>
        <button id="reset-button" type="button">Reset</button>
      </span>
    </form>

    <div class="canvas-container">
      <button id="start-button" class="button play" type="button">Start</button>
      <canvas id="canvas"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
